Case Study: Telco Customer Churn Prediction
The Business Problem
A telecom provider was losing customers and needed to understand two things: who is likely to leave, and why. Acquiring a new customer costs 5-7x more than retaining an existing one, so even a modest improvement in retention has significant revenue impact.
The goal was to build a predictive model that identifies at-risk customers early enough for the retention team to intervene — and to provide clear, actionable explanations of what drives churn so the business can address root causes.
Dataset
PropertyValueTotal customers7,043Churned1,869 (26.5%)Features20 (demographics, services, account details)Imbalance ratio2.7:1
Unlike the fraud detection project (which uses anonymized PCA features), every feature in this dataset has a clear business meaning — making the model's explanations directly actionable.
